diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 59488d9..016e140 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,19 @@
 
 A browser and desktop arcade game with a ten-sector campaign. Clear each sector, select an upgrade, and defeat the Sector 10 boss to win. Replay starts at Sector 1; your best score stays saved on that device.
 
+## Two-player multiplayer
+
+The multiplayer server offers two room modes. **Co-op** shares a team score and ends when an enemy escapes or both pilots lose their ships. **Kill race** lasts three minutes; pilots compete on kills in the same arena, respawn after losing all health, and the player with more kills wins. A tie is possible. The server simulates movement, shooting, hits, kills, scores, and match results; clients only send movement and ability inputs. This is a separate arena mode; the solo campaign remains available.
+
+```sh
+npm ci
+npm run multiplayer
+```
+
+Open http://localhost:3000/multiplayer.html in two browser windows or on two devices that can reach the same server. One pilot creates a room and shares its six-character code or invite link; the other joins. The room is capped at two players. The scoreboard is served at `/api/leaderboard` and saved to `server/scores.json` by default. Back up that file or set `SCORES_FILE` to a path on persistent storage when hosting the server. Set `PORT` to choose the listening port. Names are display names, without accounts.
+
+Run `npm run test:multiplayer` for the two-client server tests. The multiplayer page is served by the Node server. GitHub Pages continues to publish the solo campaign; its static hosting cannot run the WebSocket server or persist the scoreboard. Deploy the Node process on a host that supports persistent server processes, WebSockets, and persistent storage, then share that host's URL. The solo page shows a multiplayer link automatically when opened through this server.
+
 ## Develop
 
 Use Node.js 22 and npm.
